The instinct/observer engine vendored under `engine/continuous-learning-v2/`
is from ECC, with one local modification: the confidence-decay logic was
removed from the observer agent prompt (`agents/observer.md`) and replaced by
a deterministic Python script (`scripts/apply-instinct-decay.py`), so that an
LLM is not asked to perform arithmetic that code does more reliably.

Original contributions of this project (not part of ECC):

  - The capture-vs-judgment separation architecture
  - skills/correction-capture     (conversation-derived corrections: D1 + D2)
  - skills/delight-capture         (conversation-derived endorsements: D1 + D2)
  - commands/evolve.md             (cost-aware four-gate routing rewrite of /evolve;
                                    reads conversation candidates in addition to instincts;
                                    adds rule + memory as output channels)
  - scripts/apply-instinct-decay.py
  - scripts/verify-pending-evolve.sh
  - scripts/review-evolve-signals.sh
  - docs/ARCHITECTURE.md

See docs/COMPARISON-WITH-ECC.md for a precise diff of what was added and why.
